From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Sargison <sargo@sargo.cc>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 17:41:03 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 68/77] Plutonium: the hardware keys go to the helper's desktop
 services; the browser's media session in the Plutonium domain

In shell mode, Ash's volume, mic mute, brightness and media key accelerators
call a handler chrome sets (AcceleratorControllerImpl::
SetPlutoniumSystemKeyHandler), which posts the key to the helper
(/v1/system/key): its audio, power and media services drive PipeWire, the
backlight through logind, and the MPRIS players. Ash's own action (CRAS,
powerd: nothing on Linux; the media controller for a tab's media session)
runs when the helper didn't handle the key or can't be reached.

The Plutonium DevTools domain gains the browser's active media session
(getMediaSession, mediaSessionAction, mediaSessionChanged), watched through
the media session service (PlutoniumMediaSession), so the helper's media
service lists a tab playing beside the MPRIS players: this ChromeOS build has
no MPRIS of its own.
